TI  - Integrating Artificial Intelligence into Endoscopy Training.
PG  - 581-591
LID - S1052-5157(26)00012-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.giec.2026.01.012 [doi]
AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) becomes integrated into gastrointestinal 
      endoscopy, training programs must adapt to prepare learners for AI-assisted 
      practice. This review outlines current AI applications, ranging from polyp 
      detection to workflow analysis, and proposes a structured curriculum embedding AI 
      at every stage of training. The framework aims for both technical proficiency and 
      adaptive expertise, and emphasizes building trust in AI, development of 
      independent judgment, and deliberate "AI-off" assessments. AI can also support 
      personalized learning and ambient feedback, making it a powerful tool for 
      accelerating competency while preserving essential unaided endoscopic skills.
