OAB - Free riding in academic authorship, where individuals receive credit without 
      substantive intellectual contribution, undermines the integrity, fairness, and 
      credibility of scholarly research.Different forms of free riding, including 
      coercive, reciprocal, gratitude, purchased, and entitlement authorship compromise 
      both scientific rigor and ethical integrity in academic publishing.As a result of 
      technological advancements, additional challenges have arisen in academic 
      authorship such as the use of artificial intelligence in research.Preventing free 
      riding in authorship requires a collective commitment from institutions, 
      journals, and research teams, grounded in proactive leadership, ethics education, 
      transparent authorship policies, and open dialogue, to foster a culture in which 
      integrity is expected and accountability is shared.
