TI  - SurgiBot: Large Language Model-Based Patient Simulator for Surgical Informed 
      Consent Training.
PG  - 2250-2251
LID - 10.3233/SHTI260661 [doi]
AB  - Surgical informed consent discussions are essential for ensuring patients' 
      understanding, shared decision-making, and ethical surgical practice. However, 
      opportunities for surgical residents to practice and receive feedback about their 
      performance in these conversations are limited. We developed SurgiBot, a large 
      language model-based training platform that enables surgical residents to 
      practice informed consent discussions with simulated patients. Design 
      requirements were identified through participatory design with key stakeholders 
      (e.g., surgeons, patients). SurgiBot provides a realistic and low-risk training 
      environment, which is adaptable across surgical specialties.
