TI  - Integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) into Problem-Based Learning (PBL) Module 
      for Medical Professionalism and Ethics Education.
PG  - 2699-2703
LID - 10.1007/s40670-025-02585-4 [doi]
AB  - An Artificial Intelligence (AI)-integrated problem-based learning (PBL) module 
      was co-created to enhance Medical Professionalism and Ethics (MPE) education. 
      Developed through a structured three-phase curriculum co-creation, the module 
      combined ChatGPT-enabled real-time interaction with authentic clinical ethics 
      cases. Guided by the TPACK framework and PBL pedagogy, ChatGPT acted as a virtual 
      co-facilitator using scaffolded prompts aligned with Bloom's taxonomy. The module 
      was piloted with fourth-year medical students during scheduled teaching sessions. 
      Instructor and student feedback indicated deeper ethical reasoning, sustained 
      discussion, and improved engagement, though instructors faced challenges 
      moderating AI input. These findings demonstrate AI's pedagogical value in 
      facilitating complex ethical discussions.
